\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0452768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:14\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie opened on the AGPL PDF-parser problem and the search for an Apache/MIT alternative. Evan noted the earlier Windows path fix; code-signing cert procurement remains open.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: Licensing first — the replacement PDF parser Evan swapped in turned out to be AGPL. I've started searching for an Apache or MIT alternative. Need to confirm feature coverage before we swap again.\\n\\n**Diana**: Right — AGPL isn't acceptable for how we're distributing the toolkit.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Unknown how much rework another swap costs until I compare candidates. That's this week's task. I'd rather not guess.\\n\\n**Evan**: Separate note while we're all here — the Windows backslash path handling fix from earlier this month has been holding up fine in the build. No regressions there.\\n\\n**Alice**: Good to hear. And signing?\\n\\n**Evan**: Still waiting on the code-signing certificate to come through procurement. No firm timeline yet, so I can't say when that's cleared.\\n\\n**Alice**: Okay — Charlie, keep pushing on the parser alternative, that's the priority. Evan, keep chasing procurement on the cert, but no need for a deep-dive there today.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli open on the agpl pdf parser problem and the search for an apach mit altern evan note the earlier window path fix code sign cert procur remain open sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli licens first the replac pdf parser evan swap in turn out to be agpl i ve start search for an apach or mit altern need to confirm featur coverag befor we swap again diana right agpl isn t accept for how we re distribut the toolkit charli unknown how much rework anoth swap cost until i compar candid that s this week s task i d rather not guess evan separ note while we re all here the window backslash path handl fix from earlier this month ha been hold up fine in the build no regress there alic good to hear and sign evan still wait on the code sign certif to come through procur no firm timelin yet so i can t say when that s clear alic okay charli keep push on the parser altern that s the prioriti evan keep chase procur on the cert but no need for a deep dive there today\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee3d8c1c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"2ef58dc2a22c77d0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28737991548847297, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09263710784067569, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7417798, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee3d8c1c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1335, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:20\", \"token_count\": 372, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMake the redaction suite compatible with Windows, including build packaging. A Windows build artifact now exists, but Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; the task remains active pending that certificate.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Windows build artifact is produced successfully.\\n\\n- Build is code-signed with a valid certificate so it is not blocked by Defender/SmartScreen.\\n\\n- Signed build passes Windows Defender/SmartScreen without warnings.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMake the redaction suite compatible with Windows, including build packaging. A Windows build artifact now exists, but Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; the task remains active pending that certificate.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-08**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because Windows OS compatibility is required for the release gate.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-02**: Evan - Signing Cert Missing (Active)\\n\\n - *Found that Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; task remains active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript make the redact suit compat with window includ build packag a window build artifact now exist but window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss the task remain activ pend that certif clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 accept criterion window build artifact is produc success build is code sign with a valid certif so it is not block by defend smartscreen sign build pass window defend smartscreen without warn clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript make the redact suit compat with window includ build packag a window build artifact now exist but window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss the task remain activ pend that certif clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 activ histori 2026 08 08 alic task creat open open the task becaus window o compat is requir for the releas gate 2026 09 02 evan sign cert miss activ found that window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss task remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee4d7cc68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"id\": \"9cf930da8c6d2e36\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2812032379658172, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06539089995116748, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78476536, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee4d7cc68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1115, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:07\", \"token_count\": 532, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Issue\\n\\nPath arguments containing backslashes (Windows-style, e.g. `C:\\\\docs\\\\input.pdf`) were mishandled by the CLI's path parser, which had only been exercised against forward-slash paths on Linux/macOS.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nPath arguments are now normalized to the platform-native separator before they reach the file-loading code, rather than assuming forward slashes everywhere.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers path-string handling only. It does not cover code signing or Windows Defender/SmartScreen behavior — those are separate, later concerns for CIPH-39 and are not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat issu path argument contain backslash window style e g c doc input pdf were mishandl by the cli s path parser which had onli been exercis against forward slash path on linux maco sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat fix path argument are now normal to the platform nativ separ befor they reach the file load code rather than assum forward slash everywher sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat scope this note cover path string handl onli it doe not cover code sign or window defend smartscreen behavior those are separ later concern for ciph 39 and are not address here\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eeb39c7c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"id\": \"f22d5520af58ce07\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2721134131748795, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07628938310697077, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72903615, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eeb39c7c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 849, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:37\", \"token_count\": 390, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee3a6b908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"c466edd67f6ef08b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26236815796581725, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06539089995116748, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72198176, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee3a6b908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:22\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-38\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Build Artifact\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:05] Evan**: Path fix unblocked the Windows packaging attempt — I've got a build artifact out the other end now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:06] Bob**: Does it actually run, or just build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:24] Evan**: Runs. Installed it on a Windows box and it's passing the same sanity checks we run on Linux.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:26] Diana**: Does this mean Windows compatibility is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:36] Evan**: The engineering work for the Windows build is complete — packaging works, the binary is sound. Code-signing is a separate item we haven't even started on yet, so I wouldn't call the whole thing closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:45] Alice**: Understood, we'll track signing on its own. Good progress on the build itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 38 slack thread window build artifact channel releas date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 05 evan path fix unblock the window packag attempt i ve got a build artifact out the other end now 2026 08 12 09 06 bob doe it actual run or just build 2026 08 12 09 24 evan run instal it on a window box and it s pass the same saniti check we run on linux 2026 08 12 09 26 diana doe this mean window compat is done 2026 08 12 09 36 evan the engin work for the window build is complet packag work the binari is sound code sign is a separ item we haven t even start on yet so i wouldn t call the whole thing close 2026 08 12 09 45 alic understood we ll track sign on it own good progress on the build itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edd924d48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"id\": \"da5e0b9bbbeae005\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2617545508612861, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05994165837326582, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7326513, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edd924d48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 859, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:53\", \"token_count\": 268, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee8945628a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"b911da0ec59b38de\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25900116075675494, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.054492416795364186, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73618823, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee8945628a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:12\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## What Was Run\\n\\nA full batch redaction run was executed under the offline test harness (T027) with network access denied, using a local sample document set. The run depended on the completed AES-256 at-rest encryption pipeline (T021), since offline output still needs to be encrypted without any network-based key service.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe batch completed successfully end-to-end with the network denied: no network-dependent call blocked the run, and local policy parsing worked entirely from bundled definitions.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Noted Issue: 45-Second Licence-Check Hang\\n\\nThe run was not clean — the HTTP client attempted to verify the license key against a remote server before timing out and falling back to the cached local license, adding roughly 45 seconds of startup delay. This is logged as a known issue, not something this sign-off waives.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Scope of This Sign-off\\n\\nThis sign-off is **preliminary** and covers functional completion of a batch run offline only. It is explicitly **not** a compliance certification — it does not cover side-channel analysis, physical security, or any regulatory attestation. No patient records or clinical data were used in this test run.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 what wa run a full batch redact run wa execut under the offlin test har t027 with network access deni use a local sampl document set the run depend on the complet ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin t021 sinc offlin output still need to be encrypt without ani network base key servic sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 result the batch complet s